# Ticket Discipline

**Canonical rule**: `../../.claude/rules/ticket-discipline.md` — read it for full triggers, examples, and exception cases.

## Four hard rules (always apply)

### 1. Board-first for all features
No code before the ticket exists. If a human describes work in chat without a ticket, AI files one (see Rule 4) before starting.

### 2. Blocker tracking
When blocked on something outside the dev team (client input, credentials, 3rd-party, design, data, spec), post on the ticket within the hour:

```
**Blocked**: <type> — <summary>.
Waiting on: <@product-lead or @owner>.
Started: <YYYY-MM-DD>.
```

Apply a `blocker:<type>` label. Pause the TAT timer.

When unblocked:

```
**Unblocked** <date>. Duration: <N> days. Resuming.
```

Remove the label. Resume work.

### 3. Dual-channel status (ticket + chat)
Every stage transition, decision, or blocker is posted in BOTH places:

- Ticket comment (persistent).
- Chat reply summary: `#<ticket>: <action>. <link>.`

If you only do one, the framework is failing.

### 4. Chat-to-ticket intake
When a dev describes a feature or bug in chat with enough context, AI drafts the ticket (using `../../templates/FRD-TEMPLATE.md`) and files it. Reply with:

```
Filed as #<N> on <board>. <link>.
```

If the description is ambiguous on one point, ask one clarifying question before filing. If ambiguous on many, file with `incomplete-spec` note and let triage promote.

## Label taxonomy

| Label | Use when |
|---|---|
| `blocker:client-input` | Waiting on client answer / decision / approval |
| `blocker:credentials` | Waiting on secret / API key / access |
| `blocker:3rd-party` | Waiting on external vendor |
| `blocker:design` | Waiting on design spec or asset |
| `blocker:data` | Waiting on seed / migration / sample data |
| `blocker:spec` | Spec ambiguous, needs product clarification |

Full taxonomy lives in `../../docs/Board-Labels.md`.

## Enforcement

Violation of any rule triggers a framework-gap ticket on AISDLC Backlog per `../../.claude/rules/framework-observation.md` (F38 — pending implementation).
